.TH geectl-request-supersede 1  "geectl-request-supersede 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-supersede \- Supersede one request with another existing one. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request supersede\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIOLD_ID\fR> <\fINEW_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Supersede one request with another existing one. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIOLD_ID\fR>
The open request being superseded
.TP
<\fINEW_ID\fR>
The existing request superseding it
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
